    {
      "id": "ordered_prefix_chain",
      "finding": "Front-end twod_req.id is reset to zero and never assigned by any instruction. Native job order is preserved through twod FIFO, burst FIFO, one active reshaper job, AW FIFO, and last-AW FIFO. AXI AR/AW IDs are constant zero before any interconnect widening/remapping. Under the AXI same-ID write-response ordering requirement, each B maps to the next last-AW FIFO item. Completion events are job order prefixes, not arbitrary per-job completion bits. Downstream whole-system protocol correctness is assumed, not newly proven or measured.",
