      "id": "physical_retirement",
      "finding": "Reshaper marks aw.last at the final write fragment of a 1D job; mover pushes that flag for every emitted internal AW descriptor and pops one on B_VALID while B_READY=1. trans_complete is is_last_aw && B_VALID. FE aligns the last-1D marker and increments completed_id only for a completed top-level job. This is at the DMA AXI write-response retirement boundary; source R data have fed W, but not proof of successful B/R response, host cache handoff, DRAM persistence, IOMMU invalidation, unmap, or fault handling. B errors are ignored and R response does not gate data-path completion.",
