    {
      "id": "last_tile_window",
      "finding": "For last input IDs q,q+1 followed by the previous tile output ID q+2, ordered cumulative completion C=q+2 and next=q+3 means both input waits return while busy stays 1 until output retires. The later output cannot hold the earlier input ID waits merely by sharing this completion counter. This is an allowed counter/ordering state, not a measured reachable timing window. Source last-tile owner argument is inherited from A3; runtime/RTL mismatch and transport/cache gates still block an unconditional native correctness/performance claim.",
