    {
      "id": "cfg_mismatch",
      "finding": "Carfield runtime encodes __deserialize in immediate bit2 and labels cfg0 serialized/deadlock-safe. Fixed FE declares cfg as only 2 bits, takes only decouple_rw=cfg0 and is_twod=cfg1; twod_req_t has no serialize member. Twod module zero-defaults burst_req_o and never writes serialize, so backend sees serialize=0 for these jobs regardless of runtime bit2. Backend therefore allows pipelining and contains a deadlock/non-conformance caution. This establishes an interface mismatch and missing serialization guarantee, not an observed deadlock or proof all episodes fail. No source repair or other-version substitution is authorized/performed.",
